WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.068
 Brock, Page, congratulations.

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:05.204
You're both one step
closer to the title

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:09.008
of Forged in Fire Champion
and a check for $10,000.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.610
All you have to do now
is go home and reproduce

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.812
an iconic weapon from history.

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:19.552
That weapon is the Akrafena.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.854
 Kind of scared of it.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.556
 The Akrafena is
a distinctive sword

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:26.192
hailing from the Ashanti
kingdom of West Africa

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.228
around the 10th century AD.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.162
Initially used as a
weapon of warfare,

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:33.499
Ashanti warriors brandished
the sword in one or both hands

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:36.435
to deliver heavy strikes
in close quarters combat.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:38.705
The sword's curved blade
and dumbbell shaped hilt

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.707
were embedded with symbolic
designs known as Adinkra,

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:46.078
evoking Ashanti principles like
courage, valor, or heroism.

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.214
Today, the Akrafena
is a national symbol

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.349
of the modern day
Ashanti city-state,

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:52.218
carried by the king's
royal emissaries

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.019
at prestigious ceremonies.

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:55.121
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.690
See you in five days.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.424
 Bring it on.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.192
 Let's do it.

00:01:02.227 --> 00:01:03.729
 We're back at my home forge.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:05.899
Let's make some blades.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.333
Looks like we're getting
some thunderstorms.

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:10.035
So I think Thor's
favoring me today.

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.504
All right, all right.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.906
The Akrafena was
often made from iron,

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.441
so it's very easy to work.

00:01:15.507 --> 00:01:17.076
I don't have to worry
about annealing it.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:19.078
It's not going to
harden in that way.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.946 line:7%
Put some fresh coal here.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.281 line:0%
I'm a lot more comfortable
in a coal forge.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.616 line:0%
It's what I'm used
to working with.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:27.187 line:0%
We've got to get this up
to forge welding heat.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.156
In order to create a blade that
will have a very strong edge

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.292
but still be mostly
iron, I'll have

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.227
to use a san mai
construction-- folding

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.895
the iron onto a
high carbon steel,

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:39.131
and create a layered billet.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:42.534
But as I'm shaping this
blade, I noticed an issue.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:43.236
Damn.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.905
We've got stress cracks.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.273
Probably because of
going back and forth

00:01:47.339 --> 00:01:48.775
between thinning and shaping.

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:52.846
If those get too severe or
too deep, I'm in trouble.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.580 line:0%
 Day three, and a
bit of a setback.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.316
I couldn't go forward with
the blade I'd been working on.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:01.087
So I scabbed together a bunch
of bars of metal into one,

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:02.855
and forge welded them together.

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.858
Not seeing anything that makes
me more nervous than before.

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:09.929
So today, I am getting ready
to cut out the diamond shapes.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.198
I was going to try to
cut something fancy,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.833
but I don't have time.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.101
Time is precious.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.270
Diamond symbol means precious.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:20.640
Now I have to figure out how to
wire up my heat treating oven.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:23.242
Heat treating a blade
is a very stressful

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.744
process for the steel.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.915
With the number of forge
welds involved in this blade,

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.116
there's a real possibility
that this blade

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:32.552
could just peel apart.

00:02:36.121 --> 00:02:39.759
I didn't feel any bad noises.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.261
It's still a blade.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.263
I think I might actually be
able to finish this thing.

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:47.700 line:7%
[rock music]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.602
 Doing some blade
surgery this morning.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:50.603
It's day three.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.971
It's a very pivotal day.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.306
It's OK, little blade.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.940
Going to be all right.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.943
Those cracks are
only surface deep.

00:02:57.043 --> 00:03:00.413
I don't believe they're going
to affect my blade's integrity.

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:03.282
That's just something I'll have
to deal with via hammering.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.851
That went pretty well.

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:08.988
I'm going to put some symbols
on the surface of the blade.

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:10.823
I've really been
drawn more to the ones

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:12.591
with the diamond shape in them.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.392
Looking good.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.961
I really need to heat treat.

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:17.763
The sooner I heat treat, the
sooner I find out if this blade

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.265
really is ready to go.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.868
Woo.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.237
That feels aggressive.

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:25.671
If anything goes wrong
with the heat treat,

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.308
I'll have to abandon it if
I can't fix the problem.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.746
Got a real severe warp.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.148
Messed that all the hell up.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:38.017
There's no way this thing
can be tested like this.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.286
I really need to
get that warp out.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:43.589
I really don't want to be
beating on this thing too much.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.392
I have to really be careful
with how I hammer this.

00:03:46.458 --> 00:03:48.994 line:7%
If it cracks, that would be it.

00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:50.296 line:7%
 Day four.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.231
This blade's got a whole
lot of ugly going on,

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.634
so it's kind of necessary
to take that off.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.371
Today, I've got to make it
pretty, finish the handle,

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:00.840
and decorate the
handle if there's time.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:04.276
The major hurdles of the blade
are finally behind me, I think.

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:09.048
Unless I discover something
completely unexpected.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.417
No.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.885
I don't want delamination.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.221
I don't like right there.

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:18.424
This might come back to bite me.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.694
But I can't spend
time chasing problems.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:22.795
I need to move on.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.731
I'm not going to grind
anymore in that spot.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.367
 So my plan for the
handle is to take this

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.937
really nice looking
African wood,

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:32.571
and turn the handle
on the lathe.

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:34.507
You spin it, cut
off whatever doesn't

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:37.042
look like your finished piece.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:38.277
All right.

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:39.345
I want to test it.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.117
That works.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.787
I'm about to attempt
doing gold leaf.

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:50.856
It's going to take about 30
minutes for this sticky stuff

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.059
to be ready for leafing.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:55.127
Looks like the historical ones.

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:56.662
I built a weapon.

00:04:56.762 --> 00:05:00.967
This is the first time I really
feel confident that I can win.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.301
 Day four.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.902
I need to straighten the
blade toward the tang,

00:05:04.002 --> 00:05:07.006
so I hammered that a little bit.

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.274
That's nice and straight.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.842
So I finally got my
Akrafena straightened.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:13.079
But before I can really know
if this thing's going through,

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:14.813
I need to test it.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:15.982
All right.

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.717
So let's take a
few light swings.

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:22.989
Let's do some harder swings.

00:05:27.726 --> 00:05:30.529
I don't see the judges hitting
it any harder than that.

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.098
Let me get on shaping this.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.599
I'm going to start
working on my handle.

00:05:33.665 --> 00:05:36.235
And I'm using an
African wood, tamarind.

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.371
I think it'll suit
this Akrafena well.

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:41.441
That is what we're looking for.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:44.110
I've chose to incorporate
some symbols on the handle--

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.812
humility, and
strength, endurance.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.248
All of those elements
are in this blade.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:50.750
And I'm very proud of it.

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:52.151
It's going to kill.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.787
Time for judgment, Page.

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.955
 Bladesmiths, the
Akrafena was a weapon

00:05:57.022 --> 00:06:00.426
used by the king's emissaries
to dispatch their enemies.

00:06:00.492 --> 00:06:03.296
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon can do,

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:06.298
I will deliver killing
blows on this lamb carcass.

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:07.600
Brock, you're up first.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:08.200
You ready?

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.101
 Yeah.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:10.202
Let's see what she does.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:14.140
[dramatic music]

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:19.511
Oh [bleep].

00:06:19.611 --> 00:06:23.515
 Well, Brock, your sword bent.

00:06:23.615 --> 00:06:25.384
 Can cut around corners now.

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.587
 But blades bend in combat.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.955
 It's reassuring to hear
him say that, oh, well,

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.623
blade's been in battle.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.426
That gives me some
reassurance that, you know,

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:34.894
I'm not just out of the game.

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.528
 It's got a nice feel to it.

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:39.531
I don't see any visible
chips on the edge.

00:06:39.631 --> 00:06:42.401
Overall, your weapon will kill.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.336
Page, you're next.

00:06:44.403 --> 00:06:48.474
[rock music]

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.913
All right, Page, let's
talk about the balance

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.148
of your blade.

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:57.016
It actually feels
good for chopping.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.585
Your blade cut in deep.

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.319
And it cut through the ribs.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.524
And those kinds
of cuts will kill.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.428
 Gentlemen, to test the
strength of your weapon,

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:13.099
I'll take two chops into
these pieces of bamboo.

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:14.466
Now remember, this
isn't about what

00:07:14.566 --> 00:07:16.135
your weapon does to
the bamboo, but what

00:07:16.201 --> 00:07:18.103
the bamboo does to your weapon.

00:07:18.203 --> 00:07:20.206
Brock, you're up first.

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:21.940
 No turning back.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.845
[rock music]

00:07:32.617 --> 00:07:34.487
 All right, so, if you
take a look at that,

00:07:34.554 --> 00:07:37.756
we've actually straightened
the blade out quite a bit.

00:07:37.856 --> 00:07:39.759
It's very hard to
line that blade up

00:07:39.825 --> 00:07:41.293
when it's got that bend to it.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.794
But it did cut.

00:07:42.894 --> 00:07:48.033
And I'm not seeing any
damage to the edge.

00:07:48.133 --> 00:07:49.735
Nicely done.

00:07:49.835 --> 00:07:52.037
Page, you are up next, sir.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:52.838
You ready?

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:54.106
 Yes, sir.

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:59.111
[rock music]

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.955
 You seem to have a issue
developing right there.

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:12.591
There's a flake of metal
starting to come up.

00:08:12.691 --> 00:08:13.992
Things like that
start to give me

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:16.462
pause about whether that
blade is going to hold up

00:08:16.528 --> 00:08:18.731
as we go forward and test it.

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.633
Still sharp.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:25.404
All right, I'm OK pushing
this onto the sharpness test.

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.440
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.576
 Bladesmiths, to see how
sharp your Akrafena is,

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:33.111
I will take your sword,
and deliver a slash across

00:08:33.211 --> 00:08:34.947
these ropes and cargo straps.

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:37.650
Let's see how many
they can cut through.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.351
Brock, you're up first.

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:42.087
 Let's do it.

00:08:42.187 --> 00:08:43.054
 I'm ready.

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:47.660
[dramatic music]

00:08:51.997 --> 00:08:54.066
OK, Brock, your
blade was able to cut

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:58.370
through two ropes, two of these
ratchet straps, and almost

00:08:58.437 --> 00:08:59.838
through the fifth rope.

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:02.208
I don't see that it's picked
up any more of a bend.

00:09:02.275 --> 00:09:05.311
But overall, your
blade will cut.

00:09:05.377 --> 00:09:06.311
Page, you're next.

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:07.079
You ready?

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:09.080
 Yes, sir.

00:09:09.147 --> 00:09:13.286
[rock music]

00:09:17.389 --> 00:09:20.125
 All right, basically, we were
able to cut through at least

00:09:20.192 --> 00:09:21.927
eight strands over here.

00:09:21.993 --> 00:09:24.763
I don't see that you picked up
any bend on your blade here.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.000
And overall, your
blade will cut.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:28.801
 Thank you.

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:30.636
 Good job.

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:34.606
 Bladesmiths, the judges have
finished their deliberation,

00:09:34.706 --> 00:09:36.041
and I have a final decision.

00:09:36.108 --> 00:09:38.811
You've both done fantastic
work, but there can only

00:09:38.877 --> 00:09:41.046
be one Forged in Fire Champion.

00:09:41.146 --> 00:09:42.247
And that champion is--

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:47.319
[dramatic music]

00:09:47.419 --> 00:09:48.754
Page, congratulations.

00:09:48.854 --> 00:09:50.889
You're the Forged
in Fire Champion.

00:09:50.989 --> 00:09:54.526
Brock, please
surrender your weapon.

00:09:54.593 --> 00:09:55.761
 I came here to win.

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:58.430
But, you know, I'm
happy with what I did.

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:00.332
I learned a lot
from the experience.

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:02.201
I don't think you should ever
stop challenging yourself.

00:10:02.301 --> 00:10:05.471
It's back to the forge,
making new things every day.

00:10:05.537 --> 00:10:09.274
So I'm excited to
get back to that.

00:10:09.374 --> 00:10:10.509
 Page, congratulations.

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:11.911
You are the Forged
in Fire Champion,

00:10:11.977 --> 00:10:14.180
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:15.614
How are you feeling right now?

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:17.182
 I'm very relieved.

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:18.651
I'm very happy.

00:10:18.717 --> 00:10:19.885
I'm a metal geek.

00:10:19.985 --> 00:10:21.653
And I've never won
anything like this.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.923
What "Forged in Fire"
pretty much forced me to do

00:10:25.024 --> 00:10:27.726
is step way the heck
outside of my comfort zone.

00:10:27.793 --> 00:10:30.029
I'd like to think Brock for
being a worthy opponent.

00:10:30.095 --> 00:10:32.031
He gave me a fair
run for the money.

00:10:32.097 --> 00:10:34.266
He really made me
work for this one.

00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:38.771
[dramatic music]

